  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the presence or absence of a sure outcome (100% probability outcome) in each lottery and prefers the one without such a sure outcome. However, in this case, neither lottery has a sure outcome, so the reason would not lead to a clear preference. The individual, in contrast, does not refer to the certainty or sureness of any outcome. Instead, they focus on the absence of losses and the low probabilities, framing the decision as a risk-free gamble. There is no indication that the individual evaluated whether any outcome was certain. The justification is based on different considerations (no loss, low risk, willingness to gamble) rather than the structural presence of a sure outcome. Therefore, the information relevant to the decision reason (sure outcomes) was not considered, and the individual’s justification does not align with the rule of the reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
}

